{"slug":"linalg","pages":[{"names":["mldivide"],"summary":"Left matrix division, A \\ b: the solution of A*x = b (least squares when A is not square).","body":["The usual way to solve a system of linear equations: faster and more accurate than `inv(A)*b`. For a square matrix it solves exactly (with LU factorization, or Cholesky for a symmetric positive definite one), and warns when the matrix is close to singular. For a matrix with more rows than columns it gives the least-squares solution, the `x` that makes `norm(A*x - b)` smallest. `b` may have several columns, one system each."],"syntax":[["x = A \\ b","The solution of `A*x = b`."],["x = mldivide(A, b)","The same, as a function."]],"inputs":[["A — matrix","The coefficients: square for an exact solution, tall for least squares."],["b — vector or matrix","The right-hand sides, with as many rows as `A`."]],"outputs":[["x — vector or matrix","The solution, with a column for each column of `b`."]],"examples":[{"title":"Three equations, three unknowns","intro":"2x + y - z = 8, -3x - y + 2z = -11, -2x + y + 2z = -3.","code":"A = [2 1 -1; -3 -1 2; -2 1 2];\nb = [8; -11; -3];\nx = A \\ b\nresidual = norm(A*x - b)","after":"","output":"x =\n\n    2.0000\n    3.0000\n   -1.0000\n\nresidual =\n\n   9.9301e-16","figures":[]},{"title":"A straight line by least squares","intro":"More points than unknowns: `\\` finds the line closest to all of them.","code":"x = (0:5)';\ny = [1.1; 2.9; 5.2; 7.1; 8.8; 11.0];\ncoef = [x ones(size(x))] \\ y\nplot(x, y, 'o', x, [x ones(size(x))]*coef, '-')\nlegend('data', 'fit', 'Location', 'northwest')","after":"","output":"coef =\n\n    1.9743\n    1.0810","figures":[{"id":1,"type":"figure","number":1,"name":"","numberTitle":true,"width":560.0,"height":420.0,"color":[0.94,0.94,0.94],"visible":true,"version":6,"windowStyle":"normal","axes":[{"id":2,"type":"axes","kind":"cartesian","geo":false,"position":[0.13,0.11,0.775,0.815],"xlim":[0.0,5.0],"ylim":[1.0,11.0],"zlim":[0.0,1.0],"xlimMode":"auto","ylimMode":"auto","zlimMode":"auto","clim":[0.0,1.0],"tight":{"X":false,"Y":false,"Z":false},"xscale":"linear","yscale":"linear","zscale":"linear","xdir":"normal","ydir":"normal","zdir":"normal","xgrid":false,"ygrid":false,"zgrid":false,"xminorgrid":false,"yminorgrid":false,"zminorgrid":false,"box":true,"color":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"xcolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"ycolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"zcolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"gridColor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"gridAlpha":0.15,"gridLineStyle":"-","fontSize":10.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"tickDir":"in","view":[0.0,90.0],"camTarget":null,"camUp":null,"xkind":null,"ykind":null,"zkind":null,"xtick":null,"ytick":null,"ztick":null,"xticklabel":null,"yticklabel":null,"zticklabel":null,"xtickrot":0.0,"ytickrot":0.0,"xaxisLocation":"bottom","yaxisLocation":"left","dar":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"darMode":"auto","pbar":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"pbarMode":"auto","camZoom":1.0,"visible":true,"layer":"bottom","fontName":"Helvetica","fontWeight":"normal","tickLabelInterpreter":"tex","tickLength":[0.01,0.025],"xminortick":false,"yminortick":false,"zminortick":false,"minorGridAlpha":0.25,"minorGridLineStyle":":","titleSize":1.1,"labelSize":1.1,"title":{"id":3,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"bold","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":0.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"subtitle":{"id":7,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"normal","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":0.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"xlabel":{"id":4,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"normal","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":0.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"ylabel":{"id":5,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"normal","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":90.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"zlabel":{"id":6,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"normal","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":90.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"cmap":{"$ref":"parula"},"children":[{"id":8,"type":"line","visible":true,"displayName":"data","clip":true,"bdf":false,"hit":true,"cmenu":null,"x":{"$":"AAAAAAAAgD8AAABAAABAQAAAgEAAAKBA","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"y":{"$":"zcyMP5qZOUBmZqZAMzPjQM3MDEEAADBB","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"z":null,"color":[0.0,0.447,0.741],"lineStyle":"none","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"o","markerSize":6.0,"mfc":"none","mec":"auto"},{"id":9,"type":"line","visible":true,"displayName":"fit","clip":true,"bdf":false,"hit":true,"cmenu":null,"x":{"$":"AAAAAAAAgD8AAABAAABAQAAAgEAAAKBA","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"y":{"$":"plyKPwWJQ0Dc8aBANR/gQEemD0H0PC9B","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"z":null,"color":[0.85,0.325,0.098],"lineStyle":"-","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"none","markerSize":6.0,"mfc":"none","mec":"auto"}],"xtickformat":null,"ytickformat":null,"ztickformat":null,"ztickrot":0.0,"polar":null,"texts":[],"yy":null,"units":"normalized","fontUnits":"points","parent":null,"bdf":false,"hit":true,"cmenu":null}],"legends":[{"id":10,"axes":2,"location":"northwest","orientation":"vertical","box":true,"fontSize":9.0,"visible":true,"textColor":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"color":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"edgeColor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"numColumns":1,"title":"","entries":[{"id":8,"name":"data","type":"line","color":[0.0,0.447,0.741],"lineStyle":"none","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"o","markerSize":6.0,"markerFaceColor":"none","markerEdgeColor":"auto"},{"id":9,"name":"fit","type":"line","color":[0.85,0.325,0.098],"lineStyle":"-","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"none","markerSize":6.0,"markerFaceColor":"none","markerEdgeColor":"auto"}],"interpreter":"tex"}],"colorbars":[],"annotations":[],"sgtitle":null,"cmap":{"$ref":"parula"},"menuBar":"figure","toolBar":"auto","pointer":"arrow","resize":true,"dialog":false,"placed":false,"closeDefault":true,"flags":{"wbdf":false,"wbuf":false,"wbmf":false,"scroll":false,"kpf":false,"krf":false,"wkpf":false,"wkrf":false,"bdf":false,"size":false,"resize":false},"cmenu":null,"menus":[],"toolbars":[],"controls":[],"cmenus":[]}]},{"title":"Several right-hand sides at once","intro":"","code":"A = [4 1; 2 3];\nB = [1 0; 0 1];\nX = A \\ B","after":"","output":"X =\n\n    0.3000   -0.1000\n   -0.2000    0.4000","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["inv","lsqminnorm","lu","chol","pinv"]},{"names":["inv"],"summary":"The inverse of a square matrix.","body":["`inv(A)` is the matrix that gives the identity when multiplied by `A`. To solve `A*x = b`, `A \\ b` is faster and more accurate than `inv(A)*b`; the inverse itself is mostly wanted when its entries matter. A matrix close to singular gives a warning, and a singular one an inverse of `Inf`."],"syntax":[["Y = inv(A)","The inverse of the square matrix `A`."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"An inverse, and a check","intro":"","code":"A = [4 7; 2 6];\nAinv = inv(A)\nA * Ainv","after":"","output":"Ainv =\n\n    0.6000   -0.7000\n   -0.2000    0.4000\n\nans =\n\n    1.0000   -0.0000\n    0.0000    1.0000","figures":[]},{"title":"A matrix that has none","intro":"","code":"S = [1 2; 2 4];\ndet(S)\nrank(S)","after":"","output":"ans =\n\n     0\n\nans =\n\n     1","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["mldivide","pinv","det","rank"]},{"names":["det"],"summary":"The determinant.","body":["Of a 2-by-2 matrix `[a b; c d]` it is `a*d - b*c`; in general it is the product of the eigenvalues, and the factor by which the matrix scales areas or volumes. A matrix is singular when its determinant is 0, but a small determinant is a poor test of near-singularity: use `cond` or `rank` for that."],"syntax":[["d = det(A)","The determinant of the square matrix `A`."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"A small matrix, and the product of eigenvalues","intro":"","code":"A = [2 1; 7 4];\ndet(A)\nB = [1 2 3; 0 4 5; 1 0 6];\ndet(B)\nprod(eig(B))","after":"","output":"ans =\n\n    1.0000\n\nans =\n\n   22.0000\n\nans =\n\n   22.0000","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["inv","rank","cond","eig"]},{"names":["eig"],"summary":"Eigenvalues and eigenvectors.","body":["An eigenvector `v` of a square matrix `A` keeps its direction under it: `A*v = lambda*v` for its eigenvalue `lambda`. With one output, the eigenvalues as a column; with two, the eigenvectors as the columns of `V` and the eigenvalues on the diagonal of `D`, so that `A*V = V*D`. A symmetric matrix has real eigenvalues, given in increasing order, and orthonormal eigenvectors. `eig(A, B)` solves the generalized problem `A*v = lambda*B*v`."],"syntax":[["e = eig(A)","The eigenvalues, as a column."],["[V, D] = eig(A)","Eigenvectors as columns of `V`, eigenvalues on the diagonal of `D`."],["e = eig(A, B)","The generalized eigenvalues."],["[V, D] = eig(A, B)","With the generalized eigenvectors."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"A symmetric matrix","intro":"","code":"A = [2 1; 1 2];\n[V, D] = eig(A)\ncheck = A*V - V*D","after":"","output":"V =\n\n   -0.7071    0.7071\n    0.7071    0.7071\n\nD =\n\n     1     0\n     0     3\n\ncheck =\n\n     0     0\n     0     0","figures":[]},{"title":"Complex eigenvalues of a rotation","intro":"","code":"theta = pi/4;\nR = [cos(theta) -sin(theta); sin(theta) cos(theta)];\ne = eig(R)\nabs(e)","after":"","output":"e =\n\n   0.7071 + 0.7071i\n   0.7071 - 0.7071i\n\nans =\n\n     1\n     1","figures":[]},{"title":"Modes of a spring chain","intro":"The eigenvalues of the stiffness matrix are the squared frequencies of the chain's modes; the eigenvectors are their shapes.","code":"n = 6;\nK = 2*eye(n) - diag(ones(1, n-1), 1) - diag(ones(1, n-1), -1);\n[V, D] = eig(K);\nfrequencies = sqrt(diag(D))'\nplot(1:n, V(:, 1:3), '-o')\nlegend('mode 1', 'mode 2', 'mode 3')","after":"","output":"frequencies =\n\n    0.4450    0.8678    1.2470    1.5637    1.8019    1.9499","figures":[{"id":1,"type":"figure","number":1,"name":"","numberTitle":true,"width":560.0,"height":420.0,"color":[0.94,0.94,0.94],"visible":true,"version":5,"windowStyle":"normal","axes":[{"id":2,"type":"axes","kind":"cartesian","geo":false,"position":[0.13,0.11,0.775,0.815],"xlim":[1.0,6.0],"ylim":[-0.6000000000000001,0.6000000000000001],"zlim":[0.0,1.0],"xlimMode":"auto","ylimMode":"auto","zlimMode":"auto","clim":[0.0,1.0],"tight":{"X":false,"Y":false,"Z":false},"xscale":"linear","yscale":"linear","zscale":"linear","xdir":"normal","ydir":"normal","zdir":"normal","xgrid":false,"ygrid":false,"zgrid":false,"xminorgrid":false,"yminorgrid":false,"zminorgrid":false,"box":true,"color":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"xcolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"ycolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"zcolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"gridColor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"gridAlpha":0.15,"gridLineStyle":"-","fontSize":10.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"tickDir":"in","view":[0.0,90.0],"camTarget":null,"camUp":null,"xkind":null,"ykind":null,"zkind":null,"xtick":null,"ytick":null,"ztick":null,"xticklabel":null,"yticklabel":null,"zticklabel":null,"xtickrot":0.0,"ytickrot":0.0,"xaxisLocation":"bottom","yaxisLocation":"left","dar":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"darMode":"auto","pbar":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"pbarMode":"auto","camZoom":1.0,"visible":true,"layer":"bottom","fontName":"Helvetica","fontWeight":"normal","tickLabelInterpreter":"tex","tickLength":[0.01,0.025],"xminortick":false,"yminortick":false,"zminortick":false,"minorGridAlpha":0.25,"minorGridLineStyle":":","titleSize":1.1,"labelSize":1.1,"title":{"id":3,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"bold","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":0.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"subtitle":{"id":7,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"normal","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":0.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"xlabel":{"id":4,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"normal","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":0.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"ylabel":{"id":5,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"normal","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":90.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"zlabel":{"id":6,"string":"","fontSize":10.0,"fontUnits":"points","fontWeight":"normal","fontAngle":"normal","color":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"rotation":90.0,"interpreter":"tex","visible":true,"halign":"left","valign":"middle","position":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"units":"data","background":"none","edge":"none","fontName":"Helvetica","margin":3.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"lineStyle":"-"},"cmap":{"$ref":"parula"},"children":[{"id":8,"type":"line","visible":true,"displayName":"mode 1","clip":true,"bdf":false,"hit":true,"cmenu":null,"x":{"$":"AACAPwAAAEAAAEBAAACAQAAAoEAAAMBA","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"y":{"$":"mXxtPtf31T4uaAU/LmgFP9f31T6ZfG0+","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"z":null,"color":[0.0,0.447,0.741],"lineStyle":"-","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"o","markerSize":6.0,"mfc":"none","mec":"auto"},{"id":9,"type":"line","visible":true,"displayName":"mode 2","clip":true,"bdf":false,"hit":true,"cmenu":null,"x":{"$":"AACAPwAAAEAAAEBAAACAQAAAoEAAAMBA","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"y":{"$":"1/fVvi5oBb+ZfG2+mXxtPi5oBT/X99U+","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"z":null,"color":[0.85,0.325,0.098],"lineStyle":"-","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"o","markerSize":6.0,"mfc":"none","mec":"auto"},{"id":10,"type":"line","visible":true,"displayName":"mode 3","clip":true,"bdf":false,"hit":true,"cmenu":null,"x":{"$":"AACAPwAAAEAAAEBAAACAQAAAoEAAAMBA","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"y":{"$":"LmgFP5l8bT7X99W+1/fVvpl8bT4uaAU/","shape":[1,6],"dt":"f4"},"z":null,"color":[0.929,0.694,0.125],"lineStyle":"-","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"o","markerSize":6.0,"mfc":"none","mec":"auto"}],"xtickformat":null,"ytickformat":null,"ztickformat":null,"ztickrot":0.0,"polar":null,"texts":[],"yy":null,"units":"normalized","fontUnits":"points","parent":null,"bdf":false,"hit":true,"cmenu":null}],"legends":[{"id":11,"axes":2,"location":"northeast","orientation":"vertical","box":true,"fontSize":9.0,"visible":true,"textColor":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"color":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"edgeColor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"numColumns":1,"title":"","entries":[{"id":8,"name":"mode 1","type":"line","color":[0.0,0.447,0.741],"lineStyle":"-","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"o","markerSize":6.0,"markerFaceColor":"none","markerEdgeColor":"auto"},{"id":9,"name":"mode 2","type":"line","color":[0.85,0.325,0.098],"lineStyle":"-","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"o","markerSize":6.0,"markerFaceColor":"none","markerEdgeColor":"auto"},{"id":10,"name":"mode 3","type":"line","color":[0.929,0.694,0.125],"lineStyle":"-","lineWidth":0.5,"marker":"o","markerSize":6.0,"markerFaceColor":"none","markerEdgeColor":"auto"}],"interpreter":"tex"}],"colorbars":[],"annotations":[],"sgtitle":null,"cmap":{"$ref":"parula"},"menuBar":"figure","toolBar":"auto","pointer":"arrow","resize":true,"dialog":false,"placed":false,"closeDefault":true,"flags":{"wbdf":false,"wbuf":false,"wbmf":false,"scroll":false,"kpf":false,"krf":false,"wkpf":false,"wkrf":false,"bdf":false,"size":false,"resize":false},"cmenu":null,"menus":[],"toolbars":[],"controls":[],"cmenus":[]}]}],"notes":[],"see":["svd","eigs","det","trace"]},{"names":["svd"],"summary":"The singular value decomposition, A = U*S*V'.","body":["Every matrix factors into an orthogonal `U`, a diagonal `S` of nonnegative singular values in decreasing order, and an orthogonal `V`. The singular values say how much the matrix stretches along its principal directions: their number above zero is the rank, the largest is the 2-norm, and the largest over the smallest is the condition number. Keeping only the largest ones gives the best low-rank approximation."],"syntax":[["s = svd(A)","The singular values, as a column."],["[U, S, V] = svd(A)","The full decomposition."],["[U, S, V] = svd(A, 'econ')","The economy size: only as many columns of `U` (or `V`) as there are singular values."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"Singular values, rank and norm","intro":"","code":"A = [3 2 2; 2 3 -2];\ns = svd(A)\n[norm(A) s(1)]","after":"","output":"s =\n\n    5.0000\n    3.0000\n\nans =\n\n    5.0000    5.0000","figures":[]},{"title":"The decomposition and a check","intro":"","code":"A = [1 2; 3 4; 5 6];\n[U, S, V] = svd(A, 'econ')\nnorm(U*S*V' - A)","after":"","output":"U =\n\n   -0.2298    0.8835\n   -0.5247    0.2408\n   -0.8196   -0.4019\n\nS =\n\n    9.5255         0\n         0    0.5143\n\nV =\n\n   -0.6196   -0.7849\n   -0.7849    0.6196\n\nans =\n\n   4.9206e-15","figures":[]},{"title":"The best rank-1 approximation","intro":"","code":"A = magic(4);\n[U, S, V] = svd(A);\nA1 = S(1,1) * U(:,1) * V(:,1)';\nrelativeError = norm(A - A1) / norm(A)","after":"","output":"relativeError =\n\n    0.5261","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["eig","rank","norm","pinv","cond"]},{"names":["norm"],"summary":"The norm of a vector or a matrix.","body":["Of a vector, by default its length, `sqrt(sum(abs(v).^2))`; with `p`, the p-norm `sum(abs(v).^p)^(1/p)`, the largest absolute value for `Inf`. Of a matrix, by default the 2-norm (its largest singular value); `1` gives the largest column sum of absolute values, `Inf` the largest row sum, and `'fro'` the Frobenius norm."],"syntax":[["n = norm(v)","The length of a vector."],["n = norm(v, p)","The p-norm of a vector (`Inf` for the largest absolute value)."],["n = norm(A)","The 2-norm of a matrix."],["n = norm(A, 1 | 2 | Inf | 'fro')","Another matrix norm."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"Lengths of a vector","intro":"","code":"v = [3 -4 12];\nnorm(v)\nnorm(v, 1)\nnorm(v, Inf)","after":"","output":"ans =\n\n    13\n\nans =\n\n    19\n\nans =\n\n    12","figures":[]},{"title":"Norms of a matrix","intro":"","code":"A = [1 -2; 3 4];\n[norm(A) norm(A, 1) norm(A, Inf) norm(A, 'fro')]","after":"","output":"ans =\n\n    5.1167    6.0000    7.0000    5.4772","figures":[]},{"title":"The distance between two points","intro":"","code":"p = [1 2 3];\nq = [4 6 3];\nd = norm(p - q)","after":"","output":"d =\n\n     5","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["vecnorm","abs","svd","cond"]},{"names":["rank"],"summary":"The number of linearly independent rows or columns.","body":["Counted from the singular values: those above a tolerance (by default `max(size(A))*eps(norm(A))`) count. A square matrix of full rank has an inverse; a lower rank means some columns are combinations of others."],"syntax":[["r = rank(A)","The rank of `A`."],["r = rank(A, tol)","With singular values above `tol` counted."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"Full and lower rank","intro":"","code":"rank(magic(4))\nA = [1 2 3; 2 4 6; 1 0 1];\nrank(A)","after":"The second row of `A` is twice the first, so the rank is 2.","output":"ans =\n\n     3\n\nans =\n\n     2","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["svd","null","orth","det"]},{"names":["lu"],"summary":"The LU decomposition with row pivoting.","body":["Writes a square matrix as a lower triangular `L` times an upper triangular `U`, with the rows reordered for stability: `P*A = L*U`. Two systems with triangular matrices are then quick to solve, for many right-hand sides. With two outputs the row order is folded into `L`, which is then a permuted lower triangle."],"syntax":[["[L, U] = lu(A)","`A = L*U`, `L` a lower triangle with its rows permuted."],["[L, U, P] = lu(A)","`P*A = L*U` with a permutation matrix `P`."],["[L, U, P] = lu(A, 'vector')","The permutation as a vector: `A(P, :) = L*U`."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"The factors and a check","intro":"","code":"A = [1 2 4; 3 8 14; 2 6 13];\n[L, U, P] = lu(A)\nnorm(P*A - L*U)","after":"","output":"L =\n\n    1.0000         0         0\n    0.6667    1.0000         0\n    0.3333   -1.0000    1.0000\n\nU =\n\n    3.0000    8.0000   14.0000\n         0    0.6667    3.6667\n         0         0    3.0000\n\nP =\n\n     0     1     0\n     0     0     1\n     1     0     0\n\nans =\n\n     0","figures":[]},{"title":"Solving with the factors","intro":"","code":"A = [1 2 4; 3 8 14; 2 6 13];\n[L, U, P] = lu(A);\nb = [3; 13; 4];\ny = L \\ (P*b);\nx = U \\ y","after":"","output":"x =\n\n    3.0000\n    4.0000\n   -2.0000","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["mldivide","qr","chol","det"]},{"names":["qr"],"summary":"The QR decomposition, A = Q*R.","body":["Writes a matrix as an orthogonal `Q` times an upper triangular `R`. It is the stable way to solve least-squares problems and to find an orthonormal basis for the columns of a matrix. The economy size keeps only as many columns of `Q` as `A` has."],"syntax":[["[Q, R] = qr(A)","The full decomposition."],["[Q, R] = qr(A, 'econ')","The economy size, for a tall `A`."],["[Q, R, P] = qr(A)","With column pivoting, `A*P = Q*R`."],["R = qr(A)","The triangular factor alone."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"A tall matrix","intro":"","code":"A = [1 2; 3 4; 5 6];\n[Q, R] = qr(A, 'econ')\nnorm(Q*R - A)\nQ' * Q","after":"","output":"Q =\n\n   -0.1690    0.8971\n   -0.5071    0.2760\n   -0.8452   -0.3450\n\nR =\n\n   -5.9161   -7.4374\n         0    0.8281\n\nans =\n\n   1.2736e-15\n\nans =\n\n    1.0000    0.0000\n    0.0000    1.0000","figures":[]},{"title":"Least squares through the factors","intro":"","code":"A = [1 2; 3 4; 5 6];\nb = [1; 2; 2];\n[Q, R] = qr(A, 'econ');\nx = R \\ (Q' * b)\nx2 = A \\ b","after":"","output":"x =\n\n   -0.6667\n    0.9167\n\nx2 =\n\n   -0.6667\n    0.9167","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["lu","svd","mldivide","orth"]}]}
